Doctor Management System using Spring Boot
JPA Repository, Versioning, Hibernate
Timestamping and Finder Methods
Objective
Develop a Spring Boot application using Spring Data JPA, Hibernate Versioning (@Version),
Hibernate Automatic Timestamping (@CreationTimestamp, @UpdateTimestamp), and advanced
finder methods.
Entity: Doctor
doctorId - Long
doctorName - String
specialization - String
hospitalName - String
city - String
consultationFee - Double
experience - Integer
email - String
@Version version - Integer
@CreationTimestamp createdAt - LocalDateTime
@UpdateTimestamp updatedAt - LocalDateTime
Requirements
• Use @Version for optimistic locking.
• Use @CreationTimestamp for automatic record creation timestamp.
• Use @UpdateTimestamp for automatic update timestamp.
• Verify version increments automatically after updates.
• Verify createdAt remains unchanged while updatedAt changes after updates.
Insert Sample Data
Insert at least 10 doctor records.
Repository Layer
DoctorRepository extends JpaRepository<Doctor, Long>
findByDoctorNameLike(String pattern)
findBySpecializationIn(List<String> specializations)
findByDoctorNameStartingWith(String prefix)
findByDoctorNameEndingWith(String suffix)
findByCityIn(List<String> cities)
findByHospitalNameLike(String pattern)
findByEmailEndingWith(String domain)
findBySpecializationStartingWith(String prefix)
CommandLineRunner Operations
1. Find doctors whose names match LIKE '%Raj%'.
2. Find doctors whose specialization is in [Cardiology, Neurology].
3. Find doctors whose names start with 'Dr. A'.
4. Find doctors whose names end with 'Kumar'.
5. Find doctors located in Chennai or Bengaluru using IN.
6. Find hospitals matching LIKE '%Care%'.
7. Find doctors with email ending '@hospital.com'.
8. Find specializations starting with 'Ortho'.
9. Update a doctor record and verify version increments.
10. Verify createdAt remains unchanged while updatedAt changes after update.
Expected Concepts Covered
Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, JpaRepository, Derived Query Methods, LIKE, IN,
StartingWith, EndingWith, @Version, @CreationTimestamp, @UpdateTimestamp, Optimistic
Locking, Automatic Audit Timestamping, and CommandLineRunner.